      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): clear session labels across subscribed clients",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users clearing a session label in one Control UI client would leave other subscribed clients showing the old name until a full session refresh.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nGateway session events now send explicit null tombstones when a label or its derived display name is absent, while preserving explicit rename-flow overrides. The Control UI reconciliation path removes those fields when it receives the tombstones instead of merging stale values forward.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCleared session labels disappear immediately across subscribed Control UI clients without requiring a refresh.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before-fix Testbox regression: `sessions.changed` label assertion received `undefined` instead of the required `null` tombstone.\n- Blacksmith Testbox through Crabbox `tbx_01kwrtnmmqnd87cx8wrkhz1fmm`: gateway regression 48/48 passed across both gateway configurations.\n- Same Testbox: Control UI reconcile regression 1/1 passed.\n- Same Testbox: `pnpm check:changed` passed core production/test typechecks, changed-file lint, and repository guards.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main`: clean after the changelog-policy fix; no accepted/actionable findings.\n- Exact-head CI: 65 successful checks, zero failures.\n- AI-assisted. No screenshot included because this is a nonvisual event-reconciliation fix covered at both producer and consumer boundaries.\n",
